## Reviewer disagreements (not applied)
- The « 1er » and narrow-space thousands recommendations are right for French typography. They are not applied because the checker and ACCEPTED-ROUND reject them. Noted above, not treated as a mistake about the language.
- fr-b 5 is the one legal call I did not follow. English stops at actual damages. The Korean source says 최대 1배, and Article 51’s simple-fault cap is one times actual damages. Deleting « (une fois ce montant) » both drops that cap and fails the number check. Kept.
- fr-b 4’s suggested « (2020) » was already in the sentence next to 民國 year 109. I did not add another year. The extra-2020 warning is pre-existing; removing it would change a number that was not part of a failed check.
- Promoting Q16–Q20 to `##` headings would change heading levels against the Korean source. The layout complaint is fair; the structure cannot move.
